WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.320
The visually stunning and heartfelt Soul is&nbsp;
one of Pixar's most acclaimed films to date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.960
and hidden in the movie are stacks of deep-cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.120
references to other classics such as&nbsp;
Inside Out, Toy Story, and Wall-E. 
&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.160
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in this&nbsp;
video I'm revealing every easter egg and crucial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.480
detail you might have missed in Pixar's Soul.
There are some spoilers, so take care.
&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.360
The best place to begin our Soul easter&nbsp;
egg hunt is in the Hall of Everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.600
one of the locations in the Great Before&nbsp;
where new souls go to find their spark.
&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.640
In the sky you can see Charles Muntz's blimp,&nbsp;
the Spirit of Adventure, from Pixar's Up.
&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.800
Floating in the distance, and a little more&nbsp;
difficult to see, is the Axiom from Wall-E,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.400
one of the giant Starliner spacecrafts built by&nbsp;
Buy n Large during the evacuation of Earth.
&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.560
And the monorail is a nod to Metroville&nbsp;
and the second Incredibles movie where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.320
the city's monorail track was destroyed&nbsp;
during the battle with the Underminer.
&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.440
Back on the ground, the Aztec temple is a&nbsp;
reference to Coco's Land of the Dead and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.520
the Aztec stone structures that form the base&nbsp;
of the buildings in that movie's afterlife.
&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.560
And another Coco easter egg crops up&nbsp;
later on when Twenty Two is deliberately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.480
messing with humans in the Zone.
After she interrupts the tattoo artist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.240
you can spot a very Coco-style&nbsp;
skull in a portrait on the wall.
&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.600
The Pizza Planet truck with its distinctive red&nbsp;
and white rocket on the roof is here in the hall.
&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.640
The truck originally appeared&nbsp;
in Pixar's very first feature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.560
film Toy Story and has shown up in&nbsp;
almost every Pixar film so far.
&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.200
And resting on the side of the truck is&nbsp;
a double bass, an instrument that's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.160
prominently on display in Joe's apartment.
The garbage truck behind the Pizza Planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.320
truck is likely a Toy Story 3 reference&nbsp;
to the truck that Sid worked on as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.320
garbage collector and the one that Lotso&nbsp;
ended up on at the end of that movie.
&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.080
You'll find the A113 easter egg on a set&nbsp;
of street signs in the Hall of Everything.
&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.480
The appearance of A113 in Pixar's films is&nbsp;
a tribute to the classroom at California&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.240
Institute of the Arts where many of&nbsp;
the studio's animators studied.
&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.880
The suspended whale is a nod to Finding&nbsp;
Dory and the giant mammal on display in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.080
indoor exhibit at the Marine Life Institute.
