00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:03.120
By the way, I enjoyed how Mr Mittens&nbsp;
the therapy cat brought lots of physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:07.600
comedy to the New York part of the movie,
and the Art of Soul book reveals that the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:13.600
of the cat therapy service he works for is called&nbsp;
"Feline Better", a play on 'Feeling Better'.
&nbsp;

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:18.640
The Art of Soul book also reveals the meaning&nbsp;
behind the symbols on Twenty Two's pass.
&nbsp;

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:23.680
Twenty Two is apparently a "moody,&nbsp;
extroverted cynic who's extremely punctual". 
&nbsp;

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:28.160
I can thoroughly recommend checking out The Art&nbsp;
of Soul book to appreciate and learn much more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.800
about many of Soul's early concepts and how they&nbsp;
progressed to their final version in the film.
&nbsp;

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.240
I'll add a link to where you can get the&nbsp;
book in the video description below.
&nbsp;

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.800
Now, if you didn't sit through the&nbsp;
credits for Soul, you might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:43.360
missed out on a little post-credits scene&nbsp;
in which Terry pops up for a final time:
&nbsp;

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:44.960
"Hi!
Movie's over.
&nbsp;

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.680
Go home!"
This is a joke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.600
in the spirit of the post-credits scene in&nbsp;
Ferris Bueller's Day Off and also Deadpool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.920
which itself riffed on the John Hughes film,
and it's clearly intended for the traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:00.240
cinema experience, so it doesn't work quite&nbsp;
so well watching at home on Disney Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.200
though it is a fun little reward for&nbsp;
those who watch right to the end.
&nbsp;

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.520
Now, what other easter eggs or&nbsp;
cool details did you spot in Soul?
&nbsp;

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:10.640
And how do you rate it among&nbsp;
your favourite Pixar movies?
&nbsp;

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:13.920
If you enjoyed this, then a&nbsp;
thumbs-up is hugely appreciated!
&nbsp;

